    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "sWmiy",
      "x": 37943,
      "y": 3,
      "name": "Lesson Player · Materi pengenalan",
      "context": "Static microlearning desktop design: one concept per screen. Left: 400px explanation, one brief paragraph and an interaction cue. Right: 680px visual stage with array, selected item, instruction, output and next/reset controls. One visual interaction, no bundled code exercise or quiz. Major reasons: split layout replaces stacked form cards and lets the visual lead; Fredoka headline/numerals retain playful ZenUniverse identity; Figtree prose at 20px improves readability; warm selected item shows the changing variable while neutral waiting items defer; only the current-item card has a small hard shadow to signal selection; arrows communicate data flow rather than decorate CTAs; dark instruction contrasts with white output; stage background groups the process without boxing every sentence. ENERGY 2 / RHYTHM 2 / MOTION 1. Next iteration advances 80 to 90 to 75, updates output/counter; reset returns to first item. Footer continues to a separate bite-sized material. Runtime interactivity not implemented on canvas. Mobile implementation should stack text above the visual with 20px gutters and keep controls at least 44px. Keyboard focus 2px #C45112, logical reading order, Enter/Space for actions. Visual states loading/empty/error preserve the short reading unit, not a long article.",
